 "name": "add_blurred_background",
 "description": "The screencast backdrop — Clip ▸ Add Blurred Background. `clip` is copied onto a NEW back-most track at the same start, duration, speed and source window, so the two play exactly the same frames, and the copy is scaled to FILL the canvas, centred, uncropped, blended normal and blurred at full strength. It is MUTED — its enabled becomes {video: true, audio: false}, or the mix would play one recording twice — and it drops the original's audio.duck along with its transition, actions and label. The duck goes because it is the one field of that group that lowers OTHER material: a copy keeping it would duck the whole mix, including the clip it was copied from. It is named \"Blurred Background\". Two objects are created, so new_tracks and new_clips both come back and the TRACK holds the lower id. An error for a NEST (the flattening drops a nest clip's own filters, so the copy would come out sharp), a source with no pixel size (a text clip, an audio-only one), or a clip carrying no video properties."
}
