577	//! Adjustment clips (spec §11 GR-6): a clip kind with no picture of its
578	//! own. While it lasts, its `video.color` (all thirteen keys), its wheels
579	//! (spec §11 GR-11), its curves (GR-12), its look, its point filters (sepia, noir, vignette,
580	//! invert) and its opacity — the STRENGTH —
581	//! apply to everything already drawn behind it in its container (to the
582	//! pixels its qualifier selects, GR-13), the canvas
583	//! background included, and never to a track in front. The compositor's
584	//! eighth pipeline does the grading by reading the target it draws into
585	//! (`Compositor+Adjustment.swift`); the core's part is the kind, the op,
586	//! the rules below and the recipe's `{"kind":"adjustment"}` source.
587	//!
588	//! What it refuses, and why each is a refusal rather than a clamp:
589	//!
590	//! - **A nest.** A nest is flattened into the clips inside it, and an
591	//!   adjustment clip in there would grade the PARENT's layers behind the
592	//!   nest clip as well as the nest's own, which is not what a nest means.
593	//!   `nest` refuses it ([`adjustment_cannot_nest`]); `validate` errors on one
594	//!   inside a nest ([`adjustment_nested`]), which is what a file and a paste
595	//!   into a scope meet, because a scoped edit is validated on the MERGED
596	//!   parent (`scope.rs`); and `add_adjustment_clip` has no meaning inside a
597	//!   scope (`scope.rs`'s `refused_inside`).
598	//! - **A transition.** Both halves of a dissolve are drawn into one
599	//!   destination as a weighted pair; a pass that grades the destination has
600	//!   no half to be. `add_transition`, `set_transition` and
601	//!   `set_transition_style` refuse ([`adjustment_transition`]), and so does
602	//!   the overlap rule for any pair that holds one
603	//!   ([`adjustment_overlap`], called from `transition.rs`'s
604	//!   `check_overlap_rule`, the one placement door) — so
605	//!   `set_gained_transitions` never mints a transition on one. Fade it with
606	//!   opacity instead.
607	//! - **Blur, sharpen, pixelate and a blend mode.** The neighbourhood
608	//!   filters sample the layer's own texture around a pixel, and there is
609	//!   none; a blend combines a layer's colour with the canvas, and an
610	//!   adjustment clip has no colour of its own. `set_video`, `paste` and
611	//!   `paste_attributes` meet [`check_adjustment_video`] beside `check_blend`
612	//!   (errors, its precedent), and an action's end carrying one is closed by
613	//!   the evaluator ([`clamp_adjustment`]), as `clamp_video` closes a nest's
614	//!   blend.
615	//!
616	//! **On a matte track it is inert** ([`Project::inert_adjustment`]): a
617	//! matte group is one track, and two clips on one track share an instant
618	//! only in a transition, which is refused, so the clip could only be the
619	//! group's sole member and would act as an EMPTY matte. The recipe leaves
620	//! it out before the mattes are answered. On a track CUT by a matte it
621	//! grades only inside the matte, which needs nothing here: the compositor
622	//! weights its pass by the coverage like any matted layer's.
623	//!
624	//! Its stored transform, crop, corner, shadow, reflection, chroma,
625	//! spotlight, obscure and motion placement are kept and do nothing;
626	//! refusing them would make Paste Attributes fail from any moved clip.
627	//!
628	//! **The qualifier is its alone** (spec §11 GR-13): `video.qualifier`
629	//! narrows which of the destination's pixels the pass grades, read before
630	//! the grade. On any other clip a non-neutral one is an error in its own
631	//! sentence ([`check_qualifier_clip`], beside `check_adjustment_video` in
632	//! `set_video`, `paste` and `paste_attributes`); one reached through a file
633	//! or an action's end on another clip is inert, because the recipe
634	//! publishes it only in an adjustment source (`recipe.rs`'s
635	//! `layer_source`). Paste Attributes drops it onto a picture clip, and an
636	//! adjustment target keeps its own when the payload clip is not an
637	//! adjustment clip (`edit_paste_attributes.rs`'s `copy_group`).
638	
